# Jira description

Stories and Bugs **must** use this Markdown body. Do not omit or merge
sections. Tasks, Epics, and Sub-tasks follow their type rules (they may use a
lighter shape). Pass this string as the MCP `description` field (Markdown).

## Expand macros (required)

On Jira Cloud, each section is a collapsible expand — not an H2 and not bold
alone. Wiki markup the Atlassian MCP converts:

```text
{expand:Title}
...section body...
{expand}
```

That is how issues like FRAMEWORK-405 get the Overview / Requirements /
Acceptance Criteria toggles in the issue view. Do **not** substitute
`## Title` or `**Title**` for those three section titles when filing Stories
or Bugs.

## Body template

```markdown
{expand:Overview}
<Why this work exists, the outcome we want, and how/approach when known.
Carry durable interview or decision notes when they informed the ask.
Enough for a cold reader — not a design doc and not a Requirements/AC
substitute.>
{expand}

{expand:Requirements}
1. <What must be done>
2. <...>
{expand}

{expand:Acceptance Criteria}
1. <Verifies requirement 1>
2. <Verifies requirement 2>
{expand}
```

## Rules

- **Overview** — why, outcome, and approach when known. Brief and intentional.
- **Requirements** — **ordered** list (`1.` `2.` `3.`), testable musts. Never
  `-` / `*` bullets for this section.
- **Acceptance Criteria** — **ordered** list (`1.` `2.` `3.`), **1:1** with
  Requirements. AC *n* verifies Requirement *n*. Same count; same order; no
  orphan AC or orphan requirement. Never unordered bullets here either.
- Do not bury AC inside Overview. Do not replace Requirements with a prose
  blob.
- Prefer short prose and bullets in **comments** only. In the description
  Requirements/AC pair, ordered lists are mandatory.
- Avoid markdown Atlassian’s converter commonly mangles elsewhere; rewrite in
  plain prose rather than inventing custom clients. Expands + ordered lists
  are the supported exception for this body shape.
